# A1 privacy

Personal information of the builder and families must never enter this git repository. If privacy conflicts with any other task, privacy wins.

Before every commit:

- Scrub legal names, emails, phones, addresses, GPS, account IDs, identifiable photos, children’s names, real sibling profile names, user-folder paths, hostnames, tokens, and `.env` files.
- Do not put a personal name or email in LICENSE, README, comments, sample JSON, or commit-message instructions.
- Sample profiles use fake names only (`Player A`, `Pat`, `Jordan`).
- Device saves stay gitignored.

If you find personal information, rewrite the file and do not commit until the privacy lint is clean. See `docs/PRIVACY.md`.
